tory  introduced with the woman he wants to  marry you knew from a mile away and the  writing  that when he said when she comes around  the corner it's the greatest feeling in  the world for him you knew they were  gonna in the movie on that and her  coming around the corner so that was  strange how simple that was especially  for Tom Hanks writing it and the score  to had a lot of cheese in it and it was  kind of on repetition where you would  have oh no here comes someone attacking  and then the crazy drums kick in you get  the overhead shots and then Tom Hanks  just going in circles on this boat you  can see Tom Hanks was really concerned  about making sure the dialogue how he's  betraying how this actually was was  accurate and you see that because so  much Navy jargon is in here that it's  hard to even follow and understand  what's going on and what hurts is if you  go that route where it's so realistic  you better hope the whole environment  you're seeing visually is like that and  it clearly isn't I mean I was watching  this film and wondering why does the  water even just look so fake like the  CGI here isn't great and it takes me out  of it a lot because I never didn't feel  like I was watching a movie like I never  was sucked in so much by what I'm seeing  visually that I'm like oh my god like I  was so taken in by this whole story kind  of I just kept thinking this is a ship  in a studio lot with this fake water  around it that was really weird and it  felt like it was taking a CGI from like  a Michael Bay movie or like that  battleship movie with Rihanna and  throwing it in around a very serious  subject and historical subject and where  the writing was so focused on making it  realistic but the outside is just  another blockbuster movie it almost felt  like - with this story that it was  running on a video game timeline what I  mean by that is like it felt like it was  a mission you'd see like a Call of Duty  game even the little narrations coming  in and out from the Nazis or just from  other ships like good job captain more  food for the fish like it plays like  that and it's a just again just cheesy  and honestly I feel like Tom Hanks was  so concerned about being so accurate to  how they would be talking on a mission  like this at that time that I wish he  actually took more liberties to make  sure also that it was a little more  understandable for just the average  moviegoer and someone who wasn't totally  fluid in navy dialect and was also  concerned about keeping the story fluid  and entertaining  because the script end up just feeling  like you're reading a Navy manual and  there's no real characters here except  Tom Hanks's character I think the only  side story that worked was the one with  Cleveland who was the chef who he  actually prayed with and never ate the  food he gave him because this guy  wouldn't eat he wouldn't sleep  he was so uptight and then he noticed he  lost him which I think worked and the  whole funeral part was good but the rest  of the characters are like just pawns in  the game here they're just all walking  robots in a sense and I wish I just felt  a little more maybe had some other  characters have some kind of attachment  to you as the audience member and the  movie is only an hour and a half which  is pretty rare for something that's  based off history and it kind of feels  like a war movie that just keeps all the  battle sequences in and cuts out the  rest  it's strange in that sense maybe there  is an audience for this though I think  there's a lot of people like this movie  if they're really into action and I  think all the action sequences work I  really actually like the sound design  and the sound mixing I felt all of it  even on my TV screen so that says  something and it feels like a movie that  when you were a kid let's say you watch  movie Titanic what I would do is I would  fast-forward through the adult dialogue  and and content and then just go to the  ship sinking part and watch that I think  this felt like someone took a longer  film or film took out all those parts  about character and just threw in the  action so I definitely think those  people are gonna enjoy it for that and  just want it for that they get to see  Tom Hanks running around and all these  explosions cool but the end the day it's  not a great film its handling half the  battle here in making a good movie but  leaving out the rest and I'm trying to  say that I'm biased too because I really  do love action films and I just think  that if they just tweak the little  things here it could have been much  better and just put a little more effort  into the characters especially even Tom  Hanks's character cuz you only set up  the thing with his wife and that he's  new at this which was cool and that he's  just and he's got to make decisions that  he's not even so sure about and they  cast it around him well with just you  know these babyface type guys so it also  showed how young some of these people  were during that time in war but it  and it just felt lazy and just coming  around with all those abbath shoe at the  end I don't know I didn't really do  anything for me probably didn't play  better is just a video you throw on in a  history class to just show a battle and  this is historical fiction story but if  you're going off something old or - you  can't get obsessed with making it so  accurate and I think Tom Hanks did I  think he was he must have been a little  worried that Oh someone's gonna think  I'm taking too many liveries but that's  part of the game here in moviemaking  right so I think some points you have to  do that it's inevitable to make sure  that your audience is still engaged if  you want to see a great movie with Tom  Hanks on a ship watch captain Phillips  instead that has it all or this just has  some so I think a fair score for this  film would be a five point eight I'd  love to hear your thoughts on it down  below maybe you loved it maybe you hated  it I read every comment try to respond  as many as I can and please make sure to  subscribe so you don't miss one of my  movie reviews I also do TV reviews and  celebrity interviews as well I can use  any subscriber I can get and please  follow me at Steve rd1 on Twitter  Instagram for more of me and I'll see  you next time

